  "description": {
    "paragraphs": [
      "Luiss Guido Carli University is a private research university in Rome, Italy, founded in 1974 by Umberto Agnelli with the support of Confindustria, the Italian employers' federation. Named after economist and former Bank of Italy governor Guido Carli, Luiss is one of Italy's most prestigious institutions for Economics, Political Science, Law, and Management, with around 11,000 students across six departments and five campuses in Rome.",
      "Luiss is the only Italian university to hold the Triple Crown accreditation (EQUIS, AMBA, AACSB) for its Business School. The Financial Times ranks Luiss Master's in Finance at #27 globally and Master's in Management at #25, while QS ranks Luiss #25 worldwide for Politics and International Studies. The university operates a highly selective admissions process — 68.1% of admitted students scored above 90/100 in secondary school.",
      "The academic structure spans the Department of Business and Management, Department of Economics and Financial Markets, Department of Political Science, Department of Law, Department of AI Data and Decision Sciences, and Department of Accounting and Corporate Finance. English-taught Bachelor and Master programs are available in Global Law, Politics: Philosophy and Economics, Business Administration, Management and Artificial Intelligence, Economics and Business, Finance, International Relations, and more.",
      "Luiss has produced notable alumni including Carlo Messina (CEO of Intesa Sanpaolo), Luca Maestri (former CFO of Apple), and senior Italian government officials. Postgraduate schools include Luiss Business School, School of Government, School of European Political Economy, School of Law, and School of Journalism — making Luiss a major hub for executive education and policy research in Europe."
    ],
